Algorithm
Start.
Input the number of courses n.
Input the names of all courses.
Create an adjacency list to represent the directed graph and initialize the in-degree of each course to zero.
Input the number of links e.
For each link:
Input the source course and destination course.
Check whether both courses exist.
If valid, add the destination course to the source course's adjacency list.
Increase the in-degree of the destination course by one.
Display the adjacency list of all courses.
Calculate and display the in-degree and out-degree of each course.
Input the course name whose linked courses are to be displayed.
Search for the selected course.
If the course exists, display its directly linked courses; otherwise, display "Course not found!"
Stop.

